  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Managing disease risks and improving livestock health to secure the future of the endangered Javan rhinoceros</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to protect the health of Javan rhinoceroses living in Ujung Kulon National Park through understanding disease dynamics and helping local farmers improve livestock management practices. This will be done by (1) strengthening local health monitoring capacity by finalizing project partner collaborations, disseminating a draft of Javan Rhino Health Guidelines, training Indonesian veterinarians and conducting a health training workshop; (2) conducting a disease survey for Hemorrhagic Septicemia and Anthrax to determine the prevalence, distribution and risk factors in 19 villages surrounding Honje Mountain; (3) conducting a case control study to determine risk factors for HS and Anthrax infection in the water buffalo population and soil samples in the UKNP region; (4) analyzing and summarizing the data; (5) training and building the capacity of local people and communities by preparing a basic livestock health and husbandry manual for farmers; (6) conducting training on good animal husbandry and livestock management practices; and (7) disseminating project findings to the Government of Indonesia, key partners, policy makers and the scientific community.</narrative>
  </description>
